From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [mp] fix: a store's GPU blocks are held until it ends, and a
 resumed request reloads its KV

LMCache pull request #4955, "fix(mp): preserve and reload KV across preemption"
(https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/pull/4955), at its revision 83d9e57a2cc7b81c21a08fc66207452c5612b88f, whose base
is the commit of UPSTREAM. The port changes nothing: this is the pull request's tree.

In multiprocess mode a non-lazy STORE can still be reading a request's GPU source blocks when vLLM preempts that
request: the freed blocks are reused, and another request's KV is stored under the first request's hashes. A later
prefix hit on those hashes continues from wrong KV or recurrent state. The pull request pins the source blocks of
each store until every worker reports it terminal, and reloads the KV of a request that resumes after a preemption.
